# Project-Specific Rules (szap-projects)

## Portfolio Updates

EVERY new project MUST be added to the portfolio. See `new-project-checklist.mdc`.

## Deployment

- All apps deploy to Vercel
- Portfolio: `alexszapiro.com`
- Apps use subdomains: `backtester.alexszapiro.com`, `resume.alexszapiro.com`, etc.
- After ANY change to an app, redeploy with `vercel --prod --yes`

## Monorepo Structure

```
szap-projects/
├── apps/           # All web applications
├── packages/       # Shared packages (ui, config)
├── tests/          # E2E tests (Playwright)
└── .cursor/rules/  # These rules
```

## Tech Stack Consistency

- Framework: Next.js 15+ with App Router
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 (`@tailwindcss/postcss`)
- Icons: Lucide React (no emojis in production UI)
- Analytics: Vercel Analytics + Speed Insights on all apps
- Testing: Vitest (unit), Playwright (E2E)

## Git Workflow

- Push frequently after verified changes
- Meaningful commit messages describing the "why"
- Never force push to main
- GitHub Actions can't be pushed via OAuth (requires manual push or different auth)

## Common Gotchas

1. **Navigation links**: Use `/#section` not `#section` for cross-page nav
2. **React versions**: Keep consistent across monorepo (currently 19.x)
3. **Tailwind v4**: No `tailwind.config.ts`, use CSS variables in `globals.css`
4. **Vercel rewrites**: Don't work for separate Next.js apps, use subdomains instead
